Package: tauPanel
Type: Package
Title: Fast Tau Estimation for Fixed and Random Effects Panel Data Models
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person(
    "Beste Hamiye", "Beyaztas",
    email = "beste.sertdemir@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6266-6487")
  )
Description: Implements robust fast Tau estimators for balanced linear panel
    data models under fixed- and random-effects specifications. The
    fixed-effects estimator is based by default on first differencing, which
    eliminates time-invariant individual effects while limiting the propagation
    of contaminated observations through the panel transformation. The
    random-effects estimator uses a two-stage procedure combining a
    difference-based fast Tau pilot fit, robust scale-based variance-component
    estimation, residual-based observation weights, and robust quasi-demeaning.
    Computation extends fast Tau regression through cluster-diverse randomized
    starting subsamples and iterative reweighted least-squares refinement.
    The package provides unified and model-specific fitting interfaces,
    structural-mean prediction methods, computational controls, and simulation
    tools for generating panel data under clean, vertical, leverage, and joint
    contamination settings.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports:
